CLE F
cs6,0 $
1,0 $ Cap dry, soon velutinate or cracking up into small scales; cheilocystidia shorter than 35 µm. $ H. hetieri, p. 126
1,2 $ Cap slightly to distinctly viscid, totally smooth or only slightly velutinate at the margin; cheilocystidia often longer
2,0 $ Perispore not or only exceptionally loose (PO-1); stem bj,e fusiform. $ H. fusipes, p. 122
2,3 $ Perispore loose in few to al1 spores (Pl-3); stem base typically not fusiform
3,0 $ Spores slender, Q on average > 1.9; cap 20-28 mm broad, white to pale cream; exsiccata not discoloured to dark brown. $ H. fusisporum, p. 128
3,4 $ Spores not so slender, Q mostly < 1.9; cap 15-60(-85) mm broad, pale pinkish buff to greyish buff, day-buff or cinnamon; exsiccata often partly discoloured to dark brown
4,0 $ Spores on average > 13.5 µm long; cap clay-buff or cinnamon, but paler towards the margin; mostly in damp places with Salix or Alnus. $ H. gigaspemzum, p. 124
4,0 $ Spores on average < 13.5 µm long; cap pale pinkish buff to greyish buff; in wet or dry places with broadleaved hosts. $ H. sacchariolens, p. 120
